  "bank": "Reuse exact ranked_v1 104 physical policies, source-only proposal ranking, coordinates and provenance. Original73 prefix, round1 release89 and round2 release104. No regenerated proposals, reranking or task-dependent feasibility filtering.",
  "representation": "Reuse identical ranked104 mean4/risk10 coordinates, eight structural identities and frozen source_risk_calibration_v1; no source fitting, coordinate change or encoder reconstruction. After both shared full-source initialization updates, the dual arm keeps the complete source model for queries and clones independent per-policy mixtures for terminal decisions. Local f/g, eta and identity-mixture dependence and initial marginals are preserved. The existing no-cross arm retains its separate local-query/local-terminal definition.",
  "response_units": "Identity mapping for f,g-tau,log sigma_f^2,log sigma_g^2. Formula uses normalized control-group means and global SD, not a dimension sum. L,sigma,alpha,weights,tau are identical; changes caused by actual policy/group geometry are not response-unit rescaling.",
  "selection": "Preserve the original five arms. For dual-channel online, only the complete source posterior chooses both queries with the existing fixed order3 moment KG and complete-model terminal proxy. The independent per-policy terminal model never enters query acquisition. Each new raw pair updates both dual models, once physically and once logically. This is a predeclared heuristic; KG is not rederived for the split terminal objective. All online arms keep release89/104 and one own observation each round.",
  "terminal": "Unchanged moment terminal utility, direct single candidate, familywise delta.05 and total362. Per task, two STOP arms use360 verifier episodes each and four online arms use358 each. Dual terminal selection uses only its independent per-policy model. Freeze all96 recommendations before any verifier and complete all96 verifiers before any explicit task truth scoring.",
  "mechanism_diagnostic": "Keep prior marginal-freezing diagnostics alongside the six actual arms. Dual-channel has its own two paid calls and independent final verification; the same raw observation updates its full query model and its point-only terminal model. Report query-channel propagation and terminal-channel local changes separately. Full-versus-dual paths/raw values are expected to match under the registered paired streams, but neither arm borrows the other arm observations or accounting.",
  "endpoints": "Replicate all six-arm actual certified safe reward, false certificate and own-query-path comparisons on16 paired unseen geometries. Dual-versus-full and dual-versus-no-cross remain the registered mechanism comparisons; retain GP and STOP references and all counterexamples. Report query and terminal prediction channels separately. Score each task truth, unsampled/new-policy errors and original73/generated31/union104 feasible-bank counts only after all96 verifiers. Preserve failed certificates and empty feasible banks.",
  "randomness": "Draw exactly16 tasks once with task_configs(seed2026101601), preserving the existing shift/radius order. Fresh initialization/search/verification/bootstrap seeds2026101602/03/04/05 were unused by existing manifests at registration. Share two new initialization episodes across six arms within each task. All four online cases independently execute and pay for their search calls; task/round/query RNG keys pair equal queries, including full/dual, without borrowing another arm observations or accounting. Verification is paired within task and independent of search. No cached observations, outcome filtering or automatic redraw on public-parameter collision.",
